==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*surdak}}, from {{etyl|fiu-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*śure-||to die}}, which is from Proto-Uralic *śure. It is a cognate with eg. Estonian {{m|et|surema||to die}}. Compare also {{m|fi|surma}}. The modern meaning is by contamination from {{m|fi|surkea}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|sur|ra|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|lang=fi|urːɑ}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈsurːɑˣ]}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{label|fi|intransitive}} To [[mourn]], [[grieve]] (''very often because of someone's death'').
# {{label|fi|transitive}} To [[mourn]], [[grieve]] (over someone = ''[[partitive]]; over a dead person'').

====Conjugation====
{{fi-conj-tulla|s|||ur|a}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|fi|iloita}}

====Derived terms====
* nouns: [[surija]], [[suru]]
* verbs: ''causative'' [[surettaa]]

====Related terms====
